This is my first ever project!!!!

Question: Can a positive EV strategy still leave you worse off?
Method: Monte Carlo, 500 paths, 10k hands, absorbing barrier at ruin.
Data: My own 14600 hands, standard empirical data for 6Max No-Limit Hold'Em
Finding: Ruin rate relatively small at 0-1%, 
however 41% finish below starting bankroll when edge is small vs variance.

What's in here:
Monte Carlo Sim for Path Dependent Ruin and Risk.pdf - full 6 page write-up with model logic, parameter assumptions, and analysis
simulation.md - The Monte Carlo simulation


How to run: 
Use the code in simulation.md, tweak the parameters as you please.

Building projects like these while I explore market roles (Trading, Risk, Equity Research, Asset Management)
